

                   ADVENTURER-KINGS:  GAME 3, TURN 10

                                  FOR

                   SHAMAN UGA-BUGA MAKUMBU





                              




  Quote of the Week:

  Elizabeth I, Queen of England, to her subjects in 1601:
  "You have had, and may have, many mightier and wiser princes sitting upon 
this throne; yet you never had, nor shall have any that will love you 
better."


ACTION REPORT    

Here's what happened to Your Majesty this turn:


  In spring, Bradipo I (#2) has been informed by Uga-Buga Makumb that his 
cooperation has become unnecessary, and therefore our formerly amicable 
relations are now broken.
  In spring, Uga-Buga Makumb notified Agesilao (#9) that our friendship has 
been rendered meaningless by Agesilao's outrageous provocations.
  Stormy winter melted into sweet spring.  Uga-Buga Makumb moved into 
Plumwood (#202) with his army.  He also found a Pyramid (#40) in Plumwood, 
occupied by the Medusa.  What treasure may lie there is unknown.  Hardened 
adventurers fear the Medusa because she is a hateful creature resembling an 
ugly woman who has slimy, writhing snakes in the place of hair.  Her gaze 
has been known to turn even a hero to stone.

  Soldiers bearing the battle-standards of the Uga-Buga Makumbian empire 
marched on the Jungle province of Plumwood, a land garrisoned by the forces 
of Prometeo (#5).  Uga-Buga Makumb's forces experienced little resistance in 
Plumwood and Uga-Buga Makumb there established our reign.  Plumwood was 
found to have an income of 6 gold.
  During early summer, Uga-Buga Makumb could not cast Charm on Pascal 
because Pascal commanded armies.
  Midsummer's day came and went and late summer came.  Uga-Buga Makumb could 
not leave the 71st Skeletal Legion, the 154th Skeletal Legion and the 233rd 
Skeletal Chariots to Pascal because Pascal was not in Plumwood.  Instead, 
Uga-Buga Makumb worked hard on his Tactics but was frustrated in his 
efforts.

  In Chirfa, Cosmic Herderer Mugai (#3) brought to bay the forces of 
Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll.  Samantha (#95)'s armies took control of 
Chirfa practically uncontested.  Samantha leads approximately 1 Chariots.
  The hot days of summer mellowed into a colorful fall.  Uga-Buga Makumb 
attempted an illegal move.  He tried to use water-borne movement to move 
from Plumwood to Mare Imbrium, but his transport was insufficent for the 
task.  So, Uga-Buga Makumb practiced his Tactics diligently for many weeks, 
but could make no significant progress.
  Sageleaf was magically blessed and prospered.  The Bless affected no 
armies in Sageleaf.
  Cosmic Herderer Mugai (#3) sent an invasion force into the Jungle province 
of Ngara, owned by Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll.  Samantha (#95) 
commanded the attacking armies.  The defenders were commanded by the 
provincial garrison commander.  The armies were drawn up into lines of 
battle as shown here:

