  DEFENDING ARMY

  Samantha led her armies boldly into the fray.  No generals were present to 
lead the forces of Uga-Buga Makumb.
  Before the battle, a favorable omen manifested itself, giving Samantha's 
host an important advantage.  A giant eagle flew over her lines, inspiring 
them with hope.  Further, in this perilous slugging match, Samantha seemed 
to gain the tactical edge.
  Mugai (#3)'s troops were prepared to struggle desperately for their 
fatherland.
  Across the whole front, the 213th Chariots were arrayed against the 6th 
Garrison.  The 13th Garrison outflanked the enemy lines and charged in with 
full force.  On this field, the 213th Chariots were held off by earthen 
ramparts built up by their opponents.  But the 213th Chariots had a giant 
worm on retainer to undermine it, and the 213th Chariots broke through 
quickly, demoralizing them.  The day seemed dark for the brave fighters of 
the 6th Garrison.
  The ongoing struggle went on with a murderous fury.  The commander of the 
6th Garrison sneaked a hemp-smoking, fanatically religous assassin behind 
enemy lines.  He killed the opposing commander in a frenzied rush, then was 
himself killed.  The 213th Chariots battled with the 6th Garrison and fought 
bravely, but was steadily pushed back.
  The host of the acting commander finally crushed the army of Mugai's 
morale with one last, great push.
  Although the provincial garrison commander's host were victorious, 
Samantha (#95) regrouped her forces and prepared to fight for Ngara.

  In Sherwood, II Kahn (#6) brought to bay 
Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll.  Sredna (#99)'s forces conquered 
Sherwood without any major engagements.  Sredna leads approximately 2 
Garrison and 1 Fleet.
  With the advent of the early winter season, Uga-Buga Makumb tried to move 
from Plumwood to the Aries Sea, a non-adjacent province.  This is illegal!  
Instead, Uga-Buga Makumb worked hard on his Tactics but was frustrated in 
his self-improvement efforts.


  In Ngara, Cosmic Herderer Mugai (#3) campaigned against 
Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll.  Samantha (#95) was in command of the 
attacking armies.  The defenders were commanded by the provincial garrison 
commander.  The armies were drawn up into lines of battle as shown here:

