  DEFENDING ARMY

  Samantha marched with her loyal troops, jaws set in terrible 
determination.  No generals were present to lead the forces of 
Uga-Buga Makumb.
  Samantha seemed lucky, for she was able to convince a native tribe to aid 
her cause.  But her luck turned bad when the acting commander bribed 
Samantha's ally to turn traitor, giving the acting commander a great 
advantage.  As the battle intensified, the tactical abilities of the acting 
commander and Samantha seemed to be evenly matched and neither general could 
gain a tactical advantage.
  Mugai (#3)'s troops were prepared to fight desperately for their homeland.
  Across the whole front, the 213th Chariots faced the 6th Garrison.  The 
13th Garrison flanked the enemy and attacked with full force.  The 213th 
Chariots fought the 6th Garrison and crumpled under the heavy pressure, 
retreating in disarray.
  Having found a weak point in the line of the host of Mugai, a final 
determined thrust finished off their opponent and won the day for the acting 
commander.
  Although the provincial garrison commander's forces were triumphant, 
Samantha (#95) regrouped her forces and prepared to fight for Ngara.
  Thus endeth the adventures of Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll for this 
year.


  Uga-Buga Makumb treated with his ally Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango 
(#0).
  Your Majesty, I have news to report of wanderers in our kingdom:  
  Drago (#39) arose one morning with a desire to see Shasta, and so left 
from Cantia to journey to that province.
  Robin (#51) has arrived in Cantia from Orielle.
  Ashley (#74) grew bored with the scenery in Plumwood and left for 
Alderwood.
  The captain of the 253rd Warg Riders felt a thirst for adventure awakening 
in his heart, and speaking eloquently of Oceanus Cyclopia, convinced his men 
to sail with him to Oceanus Cyclopia.

  Cantia was raided by the Werewolf, who stormed from out of the dark and 
pillaged or destroyed 2 gold worth of property.  Starhaven was plundered by 
the Gargoyle, who came from out of the dark and pillaged or destroyed 3 gold 
worth of property.  The Icaria Sea was plundered by the Giant Wolverine, who 
stormed from out of the dark wilderness and pillaged or destroyed 2 gold 
worth of property.
  Here is the financial report for Uga-Buga Makumb's kingdom: this turn, the 
Kingdom collected 362 gold in revenue.  63 gold was expended to finance our 
leaders.  The 10th Garrison, the 14th Garrison, the 15th Garrison, the 24th 
Garrison, the 32nd Garrison, the 33rd Garrison, the 35th Garrison, the 47th 
Garrison, the 67th Garrison, the 128th Garrison, the 129th Garrison, the 
178th Garrison, the 209th Skeletal Warg Riders, the 234th Dragons, the 235th 
Garrison, the 292nd Skeletal Legion, the 338th Garrison, the 339th Garrison 
and the 343rd Garrison trained well and improved in quality.  198 gold was 
expended to maintain our armies.  Uga-Buga Makumb was left with 303 gold in 
the treasury.


LETTER REPORTS

  O King of Kings, thy heroes have travelled around the globe in
search of adventure and conquest.  I have faithfully kept their
correspondence, and now I present it to thee:


From: Guerin
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  With the coming of the spring season, I set out to quench my thirst for 
adventure.  I cast a Skeletal Army spell and the 240th Skeletal Bowmen, the 
241st Skeletal Bowmen, the 292nd Skeletal Legion and the 109th Skeletal 
Heavy Cavalry arose from the graves of the dead!  My efforts improved my 
prowess in Necromancy.
  All characters of this high level gain a new Advanced Ability: 
  NECROMANCY- "GATE DEMON" SPELL (abbreviated "GD"):  By the dark power of 
this spell, an extra-dimensional gate is opened to the nether worlds, from 
where a demon is summoned to fight in place of the spellcaster.  The caster 
has no control over what type of demon will appear.  If the Demon wins, it 
will return to the Abyss from whence it came.  If it loses, the caster must 
continue the fight at the current combat range.  If another Mirror Image or 
Gate Demon spell is cast against it, both spells will be nullified.  A Demon 
may refuse to fight an opponent of Evil to Undead alignment (50% chance).  
Note: with old Saga programs, order this spell with "GI 28".

  Gladstone failed in his attempt to cast a Phantasmal Armies spell.
  The wet spring was followed by a fragrant early summer.  I marched my 
forces into Rejaf (#1503).  To the southeast there is a Plain province known 
as Milo's Crossroads (#1504), a land of Orcs where II Kahn rules.  Their 
Orcish fighters prefer to array themselves as Phalanx and Heavy Cavalry.

  A great host of savage warriors carried the banner of 
Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll into the Desert province of Rejaf, held 
by II Kahn (#6).  I was in command of the invading armies.  The defenders 
were led by Rolando (#55).  The armies were drawn up into lines of battle as 
shown here:

