  DEFENDING ARMY

  I commanded a host of loyal soldiers.  Rolando marched with his loyal 
troops, eyes set in grim resolution.  Tiffany (#87) stood ready at the head 
of her thousands.
  The Skeletal Armies led by Uga-Buga Makumb marched into battle with a 
fanatical fervor.  Guerin's men, ill-supplied in the tortuous desert 
campaign, suffered from thirst.  I was unlucky this time, for supplies were 
running low and some of my troops had to fight on empty stomachs.  On the 
other hand my clever tactical planning gave my side a clear advantage.

  Out on the left flank, the Elite 240th Skeletal Bowmen faced the 74th 
Camel Corps.  The 124th Skeletal Dragons soared over the 74th Camel Corps 
and attacked without mercy.  The 240th Skeletal Bowmen fought with the 74th 
Camel Corps and cut them down like beanstalks.
  In the interior front, the Crack 110th Bowmen were arrayed against the 
20th Legion.  The 277th Eagles swooped down on the 20th Legion and attacked 
without mercy.  In this sector, the 20th Legion's opponents were lined up in 
an upslope position.  But the 20th Legion charged them, and because there 
was no counter-charge, the 20th Legion shoved them off the crest and gained 
the upper hand.  In spite of the 20th Legion's good luck, the 110th Bowmen 
fought the 20th Legion and managed to make some measure of progress.
  Within the interior front, the Crack 108th Skeletal Bowmen were inspired 
to fanatiscm by me, their heroic First Elder of Elvenkind.  They faced the 
21st Legion.  On this battleground, the 108th Skeletal Bowmen were slightly 
disrupted by a slippery patch of ground and they joined the fight at a tiny 
disadvantage.  Even so, the 108th Skeletal Bowmen battled the 21st Legion 
and gradually shoved them back.
  Within the interior lines, the Green 292nd Skeletal Legion were arrayed 
against the 244th Light Cavalry.  Here, the 292nd Skeletal Legion were 
inspired by the exhortations of an officer who bellowed "Do you want to be 
remembered as Heroes or despised as cowards?  Charge!  !  !"  Even with the 
292nd Skeletal Legion's good luck, the 292nd Skeletal Legion fought the 
244th Light Cavalry and were bent back by their pressure.
  Within the interior front, the Crack 241st Skeletal Bowmen faced the 239th 
Legion.  In this engagement, the contest was a straightforward bashing match 
determined by the courage of the men themselves in melee combat.  The 241st 
Skeletal Bowmen fought with the 239th Legion and the fighting here proved 
inconclusive.
  In the interior lines, the 109th Skeletal Heavy Cavalry were inspired to 
berserk fanatiscm by me, their heroic First Elder of Elvenkind.  They were 
arrayed against the 230th Legion.  The Heavy Cavalry troops charged the 
230th Legion and they wavered under the initial impact.  Here, the 230th 
Legion had to go through a ford.  But their enemy attacked before the 
crossing operation was completed.  The 109th Skeletal Heavy Cavalry battled 
with the 230th Legion and steadily advanced against them.
  Out on the right outside flank, the 209th Skeletal Warg Riders were 
arrayed against the 276th Light Cavalry.  The horses of the 276th 
Light Cavalry were spooked by the terrible Beasts they beheld.  On this 
field, the 276th Light Cavalry were held off by earthen ramparts built up by 
their opponents.  But the 276th Light Cavalry had a giant worm on retainer 
to undermine it, and the 276th Light Cavalry broke through quickly, 
demoralizing them.  The 209th Skeletal Warg Riders battled with the 276th 
Light Cavalry and were slowly bent back by their attack.
  Having found a weak point in the line of the host of Kahn (#6), a final 
savage thrust finished off their enemy and won the day for me.  The 240th 
Skeletal Bowmen demolished the 74th Camel Corps.  The 109th Skeletal 
Heavy Cavalry destroyed the 230th Legion.  The 276th Light Cavalry slew the 
209th Skeletal Warg Riders almost to a man.  The 124th Skeletal Dragons 
pursued the enemy and annihilated the 239th Legion.  The 277th Eagles chased 
after the enemy and scattered the 20th Legion in all directions.
  Rejaf was overrun by the forces of Guerin.  The battle affected the 
quality of our forces:  we could not have been better satisfied with the 
fighting spirit of the 241st Skeletal Bowmen, and we have elevated its 
rating to Elite.  The mayhem wreaked by the 124th Skeletal Dragons in the 
battle has elevated the morale of its warriors, and all agree that it has 
risen to Elite quality.  We can now raise the rating of the 277th Eagles to 
Crack, its officers having displayed especially great courage.  Rolando 
(#55) retreated to Kajaani.  Tiffany (#87) made for the safety of Kajaani 
with her motley army.
  With the advent of the late summer season, I cast a Plague spell.  Kajaani 
was hit by a plague.  The plague struck the 244th Light Cavalry in Kajaani 
and destroyed them.  The plague struck the 276th Light Cavalry in Kajaani 
and destroyed them.
  The hot days of summer surrendered to the fall.  I cast a Skeletal Army 
spell and the 20th Legion, the 74th Camel Corps, the 209th Skeletal 
Warg Riders and the 230th Legion arose from the graves of the dead!
  With the advent of the early winter season, I moved into Kajaani (#1603) 
with my army.  Southeast of here lies the prosperous province of Moussoro 
(#1604), ruled by Giovanna.  It is known to be a Desert province inhabited 
by Humans.  Their Human fighters prefer to fight in the style of Camel Corps.

  Soldiers bearing the battle-standards of the Uga-Buga Makumbian empire 
marched on the Plain province of Kajaani, a land garrisoned by the soldiers 
of Giovanna (#7).  I commanded the invading armies.  The defenders were 
commanded by Giovanna.  The armies were drawn up into lines of battle as 
shown here:

