  DEFENDING ARMY

  I marched with my loyal troops, eyes set in terrible determination.  
Giovanna led her armies into the fray.  Rolando (#55) stood ready at the 
head of his thousands.
  The Skeletal Armies led by Uga-Buga Makumb marched into battle with a 
fanatical fervor.  The army of Giovanna (#7) used magic to aid their cause.  
Magical phantasmal armies fought with hers soldiers.  Giovanna drew out her 
Sword Excalibur.  She stepped forward and challenged me to honorable combat. 
I declined to enter combat.
  The forces commanded by me were disappointed by my faint-heartedness.  
They steadfastly marched on, though with shaken confidence.  I allowed a 
prisoner to believe that allies would soon come to double my forces, then 
gave him a chance to escape.  The prisoner reported the grim news to 
Giovanna, and Giovanna deployed her forces with too much caution.  As the 
fierce battle developed, the tactical abilities of Giovanna and I appeared 
well matched.
  Giovanna waved her Sword Excalibur and her Humans were virtually 
hypnotized!  The Elves commanded by Giovanna were not impressed by her lack 
of leadership ability.
  Out on the left outside wing, the Elite 240th Skeletal Bowmen were 
encouraged to fanatiscm by me, their revered First Elder of Elvenkind.  They 
faced the Veteran 275th Legion, who sang out their fiery battle hymns, 
infused with a spirit of righteous, fanatical elan by their exalted King.  
The 124th Skeletal Dragons soared over the 311th Legion and attacked them.  
In this sector, the 240th Skeletal Bowmen's commander led his troops badly 
because he had drunk all through that night, not having expected a battle on 
the morrow.  The 240th Skeletal Bowmen battled the 275th Legion and were 
bent back by their pressure.
  Within the interior front, the Crack 108th Skeletal Bowmen were arrayed 
against the Veteran 274th Legion, who sang their thunderous battle hymns, 
inspired with a spirit of fanatical elan by their exalted King.  In this 
match, the 108th Skeletal Bowmen launched their catapult missiles before the 
enemy had fully arrived.  These attacks staggered them with telling blows.  
In spite of the 108th Skeletal Bowmen's good fortune, the 108th Skeletal 
Bowmen battled the 274th Legion and could not quite hold their ground 
against their determined opponent.
  In the interior lines, the Crack 110th Bowmen were encouraged to berserk 
fanatiscm by me, their revered First Elder of Elvenkind.  They faced the 
Veteran 186th Legion, who sang their heroic ballads, inspired with a spirit 
of fanatical fury by their exalted King.  In this match, the men of the 
110th Bowmen ran into some treacherous footing and were afflicted with great 
disruption.  It seemed probable that the 186th Legion would break through 
and win.
  The battle blazed with a terrible fury.  The 186th Legion became 
disorganized when they ran into a stray herd of buffaloes, putting them at a 
severe disadvantage.  Even so, the 110th Bowmen battled with the 186th 
Legion and gradually gave ground.
  Within the interior lines, the 20th Legion faced the 177th Legion, who 
sang their fiery heroic ballads, infused with a righteous, fanatical elan by 
their exalted King.  Here, the morale of the soldiers of the 20th Legion 
were uplifted when one sergeant yelled "Let's win one for the King!"  , and 
the battle cry was taken up by all the men of the 20th Legion.  Even with 
the 20th Legion's good fortune, the 20th Legion battled the 177th Legion and 
was forced to retreat in disorder.
  In the interior lines, the 230th Legion were arrayed against the Elite 
259th Legion, who were aided by a Thunderbird who flew down from the heavens 
to aid their righteous Heavenly cause, and were inspired to fanaticism by 
its divine splendor.  The 277th Eagles swooped down on the 331st Bowmen and 
attacked without mercy.  The 277th Eagles were bothered by the fire of their 
feared Bowmen enemy.  The 230th Legion fought with the 259th Legion and were 
beaten down like overripe pumpkins.
  On the right flank, the Elite 241st Skeletal Bowmen faced the 299th Legion.
In this engagement, the 299th Legion bravely charged their enemy, but became 
strung out and were thrown back by a well-timed, sustained countercharge.  
The 241st Skeletal Bowmen battled with the 299th Legion and the fighting 
here was inconclusive.
  The battle ended victoriously for the soldiers of Giovanna as they broke 
through at a critical moment.  The 177th Legion scattered the 20th Legion in 
all directions.  The 259th Legion slew the 230th Legion almost to a man.  
The 331st Bowmen demolished the 277th Eagles.  The 311th Legion overtook the 
enemy in their panicky retreat and were driven off by the 108th Skeletal 
Bowmen in a tough rearguard battle.  The 242nd Light Cavalry chased after 
the enemy and annihilated the 74th Camel Corps.  The 185th Light Cavalry 
pursued the enemy and were beaten off by the 241st Skeletal Bowmen after a 
tough rearguard action.  The 243rd Light Cavalry gave chase and were beaten 
off by the 110th Bowmen in a tough rearguard battle.  The 215th Camel Corps 
overtook the enemy and were beaten off by the 241st Skeletal Bowmen after a 
tough rearguard battle.
  The host of the attacking Kingdom was defeated and forced out of Kajaani.  
The battle affected the quality of our forces:  the 209th Skeletal 
Warg Riders was badly shaken during the battle and we must now rate it as a 
Green unit.  I pulled back to Rejaf with my command.

  Thy humble servant,   Guerin


From: Teleko
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  Winter melted into spring.  I approached the Crypt with every intention of 
overcoming it and whatever guardian beast lay within it.  I encountered 
the Chimera.  Raising my hands high in the air, I cast a Spiritwrack spell, 
to make the Chimera quake and shiver with spiritual convulsions.
  The Chimera moved to bow range.  Incanting a Psychic Blast spell, I 
directed scintillating, interlacing strands of magic, projecting psychic 
waves of stunning force towards the Chimera.  In its pathetic stunned state, 
the Chimera could not determine what to do about its predicament.  Chanting 
my artful words of magic into a great Holy Symbol spell, I gestured with my 
arms.  A golden mist in the shape of a cross formed around me.  By my 
special Advanced White Magic powers, the spell caused the Chimera to shriek 
in pain and scorched the Chimera with 10 damage points.  The Chimera stood 
stunned, unable to regain its balance.
  I incanted my strange words of magic and cast a Gate Demon spell but the 
Demon refused to fight against an opponent of the Chimera's alignment.  Now 
the stun finally wore off and the Chimera prepared to attack.  Gesturing 
with my hands, I juxtaposed supernatural forces of magic, casting a Hand Of 
Death spell and began making squeezing motions with my hands.
  The Chimera rushed eagerly into melee combat.  The Chimera summoned all 
its will and desperately lunged at its vaunted enemy and damaged me, scoring 5
damage points.  My spell was disrupted by the event.  I moved closer and 
swang at the Chimera and scorched the Chimera with 6 damage points.  
The Chimera turned back me with its spirited tactics.  The Chimera then 
lunged at me but I dodged the blow.  Hoping to exploit a weak point in 
the Chimera's defenses, I skillfully thrust at the Chimera and inflicted 7 
damage points.  The Chimera dropped to the ground, fatally pierced.  I 
sacked the treasure room of the Chimera.  I walked over to a mound of 
treasure and secured the Huge Hoard of Gold.  I found 38 gold in the 
treasure of the Chimera.
  I saw nothing special while scouting out the Crypt.
  The wet spring was followed by a sultry early summer.  I flew into 
Alderwood.  Turning to the southwest, one can see a prosperous Sea area, 
which is known as the Aries Sea (#1802).  It is populated by no races and 
no one rules there.  West of here is Chandrapur (#1801), a Plain province 
ruled by Giovanna, where Humans dwell.  Their Human warriors array 
themselves as Legion.  To the north is a forbidding mass of glaciers which 
has no end.

  A conquering horde owing their allegiance to 
Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll invaded the province of Alderwood, a 
Forest area ruled by Prometeo (#5).  I commanded the invading armies.  The 
defenders were led by Marlon (#68).  The armies were drawn up into lines of 
battle as shown here:

  ATTACKING ARMY, Battle of Alderwood (0101):

