  DEFENDING ARMY

  Standing tall with my warriors was I.  Marlon stood determinedly at the 
head of his thousands.
  The battle was a fair fight, as no luck of great importance seemed to 
influence the overall result of the engagement before it started.  Tactical 
supremacy was clearly guaranteed by Teleko's powerful tactical mind.

  Out on the left outside flank, the 326th Dragons were arrayed against the 
Veteran 258th Legion.  The 326th Dragons soared over the 258th Legion and 
attacked them.  The 319th Eagles swooped down on the 258th Legion and 
attacked without mercy.  On this battleground, the clever commander of the 
326th Dragons thought of an idea.  He dragged a few monks out of a nearby 
monastery and lined them up as human shields.  The 326th Dragons fought with 
the 258th Legion and determinedly plowed into their opponents.
  In the interior lines, the Veteran 323rd Trolls were arrayed against the 
232nd Legion.  The 321st Eagles soared over the 232nd Legion and attacked 
without mercy.  The 323rd Trolls battled with the 232nd Legion and viciously 
crushed them.
  Out on the right outside wing, the Crack 320th Eagles were encouraged to 
fanatical anger by me, their glorious Ace of Eagles.  They were arrayed 
against the Crack 257th Legion.  The 320th Eagles soared over the 257th 
Legion and attacked them.  The 322nd Eagles swooped down on the 257th Legion 
and attacked them.  In this sector, a few soldiers of the 257th Legion 
panicked; however, they were quickly executed by roving security police, and 
the battle proceeded with little disruption.  It seemed that the 320th 
Eagles would break through and win.
  But the battle was not yet done.  The 320th Eagles carelessly blundered 
into a nest of booby traps and lost some of their best front-line troops.  
Even so, the 320th Eagles battled the 257th Legion and was able to make some 
progress.
  The host of Teleko broke the army of Prometeo (#5)'s fighting spirit with 
one last, great push.  The 326th Dragons scattered the 258th Legion in all 
directions.  The 323rd Trolls annihilated the 232nd Legion.  The 320th 
Eagles slew the 257th Legion almost to a man.
  Alderwood was overrun by Teleko's forces in a bloody campaign.  The battle 
affected the quality of our forces:  we could not have been more pleased 
with the fighting spirit of the 322nd Eagles, and we have elevated its 
ranking to Elite.  His forces completely destroyed, Marlon (#68) escaped 
alone to Mare Imbrium.
  Midsummer's night came and went and late summer arrived.  I recruited 
enough men in Alderwood to create the 234th Dragons for the army of Teleko.
  With the advent of the fall season I flew over to Chandrapur.  To the 
north, the landscape is scarred by an unending expanse of frigid ice.

  A great host of warriors carried the banner of 
Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll into the Plain province of Chandrapur, 
held by Giovanna (#7).  Chandrapur was overrun and occupied by Teleko's 
host.  Chandrapur was found to have an income of 3 gold.
  The fall cooled into the stillness of early winter.  I flew into Jaguardo. 
To the north icy wastes extend to meet the horizon.

  A host of savage warriors carried the banner of 
Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll into the Desert province of Jaguardo, 
held by Giovanna.  Teleko's forces took Jaguardo without any major battles.  
Jaguardo was discovered to have an income of 1 gold.

  Thy humble servant,   Teleko


From: Gridley, Squire to Melantheus
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  In spring, Melantheus tried to practice his Sageness, but the task was 
beyond his natural aptitude.  He invented nothing valuable in his sagely 
experiments.
  With the advent of the early summer season, Melantheus tried to improve 
his Sageness, but the task was beyond his aptitude.  He invented nothing 
valuable in his sagely researches.
  With the coming of the late summer season Melantheus tried to improve his 
Sageness, but the task seemed beyond his aptitude.  He invented nothing 
valuable in his sagely experiments.
  Talking to some friendly farmers, Melantheus heard a rumor about a Maze in 
Starhaven (#701), occupied by the Troll.  They say that the Troll owns the 
Large Hoard of Gold.
  With the coming of the fall season, Melantheus was tutored in the art of 
Sageness by Amalric.  Melantheus tried to improve his Sageness, but the task 
seemed beyond his ability.  He invented nothing in his sagely researches.
  With the advent of the early winter season, Melantheus was tutored in 
Sageness by Amalric.  Melantheus tried to improve his Sageness, but the task 
seemed beyond his natural ability.  He discovered nothing in his sagely 
researches.

  Thy humble servant,   Gridley, Squire to Melantheus


From: Tao-Li
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  With the advent of the spring season I prepared to quench my thirst for 
glory.  I attempted an illegal move.  I could not move to the Angel Sea 
because my fleets couldn't enter the parted sea.  So, I worked hard on my 
Meleeing but was thwarted in my self-improvement efforts.
  During early summer, I could find no soldiers in Kildare for the requested 
Whales troops.  Instead, I practiced my Tactics well, and even consulted a 
palm reader, but could not improve my Tactics.
  With the advent of the late summer season, I attempted an illegal move.  I 
tried to move from Kildare to the Giant Turtle Sea, a non-adjacent province. 
Instead, I sailed into the Crabman Sea (#1003) with my formidable command.  
To the northwest there lies a Sea province known as the Cider Sea (#902), an 
area of no races where no one rules.
  Tao-Li's naval forces took control of the Crabman Sea practically 
uncontested.  The Crabman Sea was found to have an income of 1 gold.
  With the advent of the fall season, I attempted an illegal move.  I tried 
to move from the Crabman Sea to the Cannibal Sea, a non-adjacent province.  
Instead, I moved into the Giant Turtle Sea (#1002) with my redoubtable 
Fleet.  Northwest of here is the Cognac Sea (#1001), a prosperous Sea 
province ruled by no one, where no races dwell.
  The Giant Turtle Sea was conquered and occupied by Tao-Li's fleet.  The 
Giant Turtle Sea was discovered to have an income of 1 gold.
  With the advent of the early winter season I could find no soldiers in the 
Giant Turtle Sea for the requested Mermen troops.  Instead, I practiced my 
Psychic Magic for months, but could make no progress.

  Thy humble servant,   Tao-Li


From: Lallipugh
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  With the coming of the spring season, I prepared to quench my thirst for 
glory.  I tried to practice my Sageness, but the task seemed beyond my 
natural ability.  I discovered nothing in my sagely experiments.
  With the advent of the early summer season, I tried to improve my Sageness,
but the task was beyond my ability.  I invented nothing in my sagely 
researches.
  With the coming of the late summer season, I tried to practice my Sageness,
but the task seemed beyond my aptitude.  I discovered nothing worthy of note 
in my sagely researches.
  With the advent of the fall season, I tried to improve my Sageness, but 
the task was beyond my natural aptitude.  I invented nothing in my sagely 
researches.
  With the advent of the early winter season I was instructed in Sageness by 
Amalric.  I tried to improve my Sageness, but the task seemed beyond my 
ability.  My experience raised my aptitude in Sageness.  I invented nothing 
valuable in my sagely experiments.

  Thy humble servant,   Lallipugh


From: Watson, Squire to Amalric
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  With the coming of the spring season, Amalric prepared to quench his 
thirst for glory.  He tried to improve his Sageness, but the task seemed 
beyond his natural ability.  He invented nothing valuable in his sagely 
researches.
  With the advent of the early summer season, Amalric tried to practice his 
Sageness, but the task was beyond his natural aptitude.  He discovered 
nothing valuable in his sagely researches.
  With the coming of the late summer season, Amalric tried to practice his 
Sageness, but the task seemed beyond his aptitude.  He invented nothing in 
his sagely researches.
  With the coming of the fall season Amalric practiced his Sageness and his 
skill in Sageness went up.
  Congratulations!  You have attained level 7 in Sageness.  Your characters 
of this high level gain a new Advanced Ability: 
  SAGE'S UNIVERSITY:  The Sage gains an additional plus 1 level when 
researching inventions if he is at his University (the location is shown in 
the Characters listing).  All percentage bonuses are cumulative.
  Amalric discovered nothing in his sagely researches.
  In early winter, Amalric tried to practice his Sageness, but the task was 
beyond his natural aptitude.  In his sagely researches, he discovered a 
fabulous invention called the Umbrella!  The following benefits are 
conferred by the Umbrella:
  The Umbrella protects people from getting soaked in the rain, thus curbing 
pneumonia and other diseases.  Healthy people are working, tax-paying 
people.  Your revenues are raised by an average of 1% each gameturn.


  Thy humble servant,   Watson, Squire to Amalric


From: Odysseus
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  In spring, I rode my flying armies into Bir Nzaran.  I was informed by 
some sheepherders of a perilous feature in Bir Nzaran, a Cavern (#43) where 
dwells the Ice Devil.  Legend says the Huge Hoard of Gold is hidden here.  
Legend has it that the Ice Devil is an extraordinarily cruel, cold and very 
powerful devil with magical powers.

  An army coming from the empire of Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll 
invaded Bir Nzaran, hoping to subjugate that province owned by II Kahn (#6) 
and made up of great Deserts.  Odysseus's forces encountered little 
opposition in Bir Nzaran and I there established our rule.  Bir Nzaran was 
found to have a tax base of 5 gold.
  Windy spring blossomed into early summer.  I rode my flying armies over to 
Ravenwood.

  A conquering horde owing their allegiance to 
Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll invaded the province of Ravenwood, a 
Forest area owned by II Kahn.  I commanded the invading armies.  The 
defending forces were led by Kahn.  The armies were drawn up into lines of 
battle as shown here:

  ATTACKING ARMY, Battle of Ravenwood (1102):

   91st     123rd     102nd     249th   
 Dragons    Eagles    Eagles   Dragons  
 01     01        01     01 
                                        
 334th/C   198th/V   206th/V   333rd/V  
  Bowmen    Trolls   Dragons    Bowmen  
 }}}01}}}     01     01  }}}01}}} 
----------------------------------------
 }}}06}}}     06        06        06    
 188th/V   220th/V   218th/V    16th/A  
  Bowmen    Lt Cav    Legion    Legion  
                                        
  DEFENDING ARMY

  I led a host of loyal soldiers into the battle.  II Kahn stood ready at 
the head of his thousands.
  I was unlucky this day, for many of my skirmishers became scattered in a 
swamp.  Kahn thus gained a significant edge.  As the desperate battle 
developed, the tactical wit of Kahn and I seemed evenly matched.

  Out on the left outside flank, the Crack 334th Bowmen faced the Veteran 
188th Bowmen.  The 91st Dragons soared over the 188th Bowmen and attacked 
without mercy.  The 91st Dragons were decimated by the bolts loosed by those 
dangerous Bowmen.  On this battleground, the 188th Bowmen expected to have 
the advantage because they had constructed prepared defenses, but were 
chagrined to find out that their enemy had done the same.  The 334th Bowmen 
battled with the 188th Bowmen and managed to make some progress.
  Within the interior lines, the Veteran 198th Trolls faced the Veteran 
220th Light Cavalry.  The 123rd Eagles soared over the 220th Light Cavalry 
and attacked them.  In this area, some soldiers of the 198th Trolls noticed 
the presence of an encampment of trollops behind their opponents, so they 
lustily concentrated their efforts to break through.
  But might defeat now be snatched from the jaws of victory?  The commander 
of the 220th Light Cavalry decided on a charge.  He moved to the front and 
shouted "Smash the cowards!"   and the 220th Light Cavalry charged 
valiantly.  Even with the 220th Light Cavalry's good luck, the 198th Trolls 
battled with the 220th Light Cavalry and gradually shoved them back.
  In the interior front, the Veteran 206th Dragons faced the Veteran 218th 
Legion.  The 206th Dragons swooped down on the 218th Legion and attacked 
without mercy.  The 102nd Eagles soared over the 218th Legion and attacked 
without mercy.  On this field, the soldiers of the 218th Legion were delayed 
by a muddy field.  The 206th Dragons fought with the 218th Legion and moved 
ahead slowly, battled for every foot of their advance.
  Out on the right flank, the Veteran 333rd Bowmen faced the 16th Legion, 
who were blessed by a band of priests sent by the League of Pagan Clerics, 
which aroused them to a fanatical zeal.  The 249th Dragons swooped down on 
the 16th Legion and attacked without mercy.  Here, an officer of the 16th 
Legion perceived a gap in the enemy lines which had opened when they moved 
around a wide rock formation.  Charging into the gap, the 16th Legion gained 
a considerable advantage.
  But would victory yet be snatched from the jaws of defeat?  The 333rd 
Bowmen used wide-headed arrows to slash apart the enemy's catapult engines.  
The 333rd Bowmen fought the 16th Legion and plowed into their opponents.
  The forces of Odysseus broke through the lines of their enemy and were 
victorious.  The 334th Bowmen scattered the 188th Bowmen in all directions.  
The 333rd Bowmen destroyed the 16th Legion.  The 91st Dragons pursued the 
enemy and annihilated the 218th Legion.  The 102nd Eagles gave chase and 
demolished the 220th Light Cavalry.
  Odysseus's campaign accomplished the conquest of Ravenwood.  The battle 
affected the quality of our forces:  the 206th Dragons proved its mettle in 
the fight and we now rate it a Crack unit.
  With the advent of the late summer season, I flew over to Peachwood.
  The sultry days of summer mellowed into fall.  Odysseus's Tornado spell 
fizzled and I was left covered with psycho-kinetic slime.
  During early winter, Odysseus's attempted cast of the Tornado spell didn't 
work.

  Thy humble servant,   Odysseus


From: Elmer
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  With the coming of the spring season, I prepared to quench my thirst for 
glory.  I enlisted enough men in Chaco to form the 338th Garrison and the 
339th Garrison for the army of the provincial garrison commander.  Elmer's 
efforts raised my prowess in Druidism.
  The wet spring blossomed into early summer.  I journeyed to Balmwood.
  In late summer, I recruited the 10th Garrison from among the people of 
Balmwood, to serve under the provincial garrison commander.
  With the coming of the fall season, I cast a Bless spell.  Ngara was 
magically blessed and prospered.  The Bless affected no armies in Ngara.
  The fall season darkened into a frigid early winter.  I failed in my 
ineffectual attempt to cast a Bless spell.

  Thy humble servant,   Elmer


From: Presto
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  In spring, I travelled to Hollabrand.  While adventuring, I saw no 
monster.
  With the coming of the early summer season I explored Hollabrand well and 
now 100% of it has been explored.  During my travels, I was ambushed, tied 
up and severely beaten by wild-eyed soldiers.  I escaped.  A King's Marshal 
caught up with me.  But I was obviously no wanted spy, so I got off the 
hook.

  Midsummer's day came and went and late summer came.  I journeyed to the 
Ark Royal Sea.  During my travels this season, I was challenged by a local 
sheriff who evidently believed I was a spy.  But when I was taken to the 
local sheriff, I showed him the official seal of Uga-Buga Makumb, and was 
let go.

  During fall, I travelled about the Ark Royal Sea, exploring its features.  
After my exploration efforts, 100% of it has been explored to date.  In my 
travels, I saw no monsters.
  With the coming of the early winter season, I moved into the Plesiosaurus 
Sea.  I discovered a heretofore unknown Tomb (#119) in the Plesiosaurus Sea, 
held by the Mummy.  Legend says the Obsidian Vermin is hidden here.  The 
Mummy is a horribly strong undead Pharoah of ancient times which has been 
wrapped in linen bandages and laid to rest, but cannot pass to the next 
world because of some terrible misdeed committed by the Pharoah in his 
lifetime.  I saw no monsters.

  Thy humble servant,   Presto


From: Tattoo, Squire to Magnus
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  In spring, Magnus tried to practice his Sageness, but the task was beyond 
his natural aptitude.  He discovered nothing in his sagely researches.
  With the coming of the early summer season Magnus invented nothing in his 
sagely researches.
  Midsummer's day came and went and late summer came.  Magnus discovered 
nothing in his sagely researches.
  During fall, Magnus was tutored in the art of Sageness by Amalric.  Magnus 
tried to improve his Sageness, but the task seemed beyond his ability.  His 
efforts improved his aptitude in Sageness.  He discovered nothing in his 
sagely researches.
  With the advent of the early winter season Magnus was instructed in 
