  All characters of this high level are awarded the following Advanced 
Ability: 
  SAGE'S UNIVERSITY:  The Sage gains an additional plus 1 level when 
researching inventions if he is at his University (the location is shown in 
the Characters listing).  All percentage bonuses are cumulative.
  Magnus discovered nothing valuable in his sagely researches.

  Thy humble servant,   Tattoo, Squire to Magnus


From: Gridley, Squire to Clarambald
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  In spring, Clarambald hired the 212th Camel Corps, a mercenary army which 
had made its way to Cherrywood.
  With the coming of the early summer season Clarambald moved into Amberleaf 
(#401) with her high-spirited army.
  Midsummer's day came and went and late summer came.  Clarambald assigned 
the 18th Garrison to the provincial garrison commander in Amberleaf.
  During fall, Clarambald announced a call for recruits in Amberleaf and was 
able to enlist the 24th Garrison and the 32nd Garrison to fight for 
Clarambald.
  With the advent of the early winter season Clarambald moved into 
Belladonna (#302) with her high-spirited army.  She discovered a feature in 
Belladonna: a Hollow Tree (#122) occupied by the Treant.  What treasure may 
lie there is unknown.  The Treant is a large tree capable of moving its 
limbs and arms much as a man does.

  Thy humble servant,   Gridley, Squire to Clarambald


From: Constantine
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  With the coming of the spring season, I set out to quench my thirst for 
adventure.  I cast a Kill Enemy spell and Kokocala (#10) was magically 
killed by a dark Necromantic spell!  Thus did Kokocala die, a brave end by 
any standard.  His possessions were burned with Kokocala on the funeral 
pyre.
  The wet spring blossomed into early summer.  I marched my command into 
Starhaven (#701).  I also found a Pyramid (#4) in Starhaven, inhabited by 
the Gargoyle.  What treasure may lie there is unknown.  The Gargoyle is an 
ugly and evil winged humanoid monster.  It is extremely vicious and cruel.
  Midsummer's night came and went and late summer arrived.  I cast a 
Skeletal Army spell and the 250th Skeletal Bowmen, the 172nd Skeletal Legion,
the 191st Skeletal Legion and the 192nd Skeletal Chariots arose from the 
graves of the dead!
  With the coming of the fall season, I marched on Berga (#602) with my 
formidable forces.  I made some side trips while marching through Berga and 
now 100% of Berga has been explored.  I was told by some peasants of a 
feature in Berga previously unknown to us, an Altar (#97) inhabited by 
the Renegade Swordsman.  Legend says the Large Hoard of Gold is hidden here. 
Mercenaries describe the Renegade Swordsman as a famous swordsman who has 
chosen to distance himself from his fellow man and build his power on the 
strength of his swordsmanship.
  During early winter, I moved into Silvermist (#502) with my redoubtable 
army.

  Thy humble servant,   Constantine


From: Montgomery, Squire to Pascal
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  With the advent of the spring season, Pascal set out to quench his thirst 
for glory.  He cast a Plague spell.  Orielle was hit by a plague.  The 
plague struck the 225th Skeletal Legion in Orielle and destroyed them.  
Pascal's efforts improved his prowess in Necromancy.
  All characters of this exalted level are awarded the following Advanced 
Ability: 
  NECROMANCY- "GATE DEMON" SPELL (abbreviated "GD"):  By the dark power of 
this spell, an extra-dimensional gate is opened to the nether worlds, from 
where a demon is summoned to fight in place of the spellcaster.  The caster 
has no control over what type of demon will appear.  If the Demon wins, it 
will return to the Abyss from whence it came.  If it loses, the caster must 
continue the fight at the current combat range.  If another Mirror Image or 
Gate Demon spell is cast against it, both spells will be nullified.  A Demon 
may refuse to fight an opponent of Evil to Undead alignment (50% chance).  
Note: with old Saga programs, order this spell with "GI 28".

  The wet spring was followed by early summer.  Pascal marched on Tesawa 
(#203) with his command.

  A conquering horde owing their allegiance to 
Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll invaded the province of Tesawa, a 
Mountain area ruled by Prometeo (#5).  Tesawa was overrun and occupied by 
Pascal's host.  Tesawa was discovered to have an income of 1 gold.
  In late summer, Pascal recruited the 235th Garrison from among the people 
of Tesawa, to serve under the provincial garrison commander.
  With the coming of the fall season Pascal boldly marched his forces into 
Orielle (#204).  Pascal made some side trips while marching through Orielle 
and now 100% of Orielle has been explored.
  The fall season cooled into a frigid early winter.  Pascal cast a Skeletal 
Army spell and the 225th Skeletal Legion arose from the graves of the dead!

  Thy humble servant,   Montgomery, Squire to Pascal


From: Gunga Din, Squire to Alaric
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  With the coming of the spring season Alaric set out to quench his thirst 
for glory.  He cast a Plague spell.  Sageleaf was hit by a plague.  The 
Plague affected no armies in Sageleaf.
  With the coming of the early summer season, Alaric cast a Skeletal Army 
spell and no skeletons answered the spell's call.
  In late summer, Alaric moved into Sageleaf (#1602) with his redoubtable 
army.  Turning to the northeast, one can see a Desert area, which is known 
as Jaguardo (#1701).  It is populated by Humans and Giovanna rules there.  
Their Human warriors traditionally fight as Camel Corps.  East of here is 
Tigerhome (#1702), a rich Forest area owned by Giovanna, where Trolls dwell. 
They can muster a host of Trolls to defend their province.  To the southeast 
there lies a Mountain province known as Pearlgate (#1703), a rich land of 
Humans where Giovanna rules.  Their Human warriors traditionally array 
themselves in the style of Legion and Light Cavalry.

  An army coming from the empire of Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll 
invaded Sageleaf, hoping to conquer that province ruled by Giovanna (#7) and 
made up of extensive Forests.  Alaric's armies took possession of Sageleaf 
practically uncontested.  Sageleaf was found to have an income of 5 gold.
  The summer mellowed into fall.  Alaric tried a Skeletal Army spell, but 
bungled it.
  With the coming of the early winter season, Alaric marched his command 
into Tigerhome (#1702).  Southeast of here is Marigold (#1803), a poor 
Forest area owned by Giovanna, where Humans dwell.  Their Human warriors 
traditionally fight in the style of Legion.

  A conquering horde owing their allegiance to 
Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll invaded the province of Tigerhome, a 
Forest area owned by Giovanna.  Tigerhome was conquered and occupied by 
Alaric's host.  Tigerhome was discovered to have an income of 10 gold.

  Thy humble servant,   Gunga Din, Squire to Alaric


From: Mortimer, Squire to Marlboro
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  With the advent of the spring season Marlboro prepared to quench his 
thirst for adventure.  He announced a plea for volunteers in Berga and was 
able to enlist the 33rd Garrison to fight for the provincial garrison 
commander.
  In early summer, Marlboro travelled to Limerick.
  Midsummer's night passed and late summer arrived.  Marlboro levied the 
14th Garrison in Limerick to serve the provincial garrison commander.
  With the advent of the fall season, Marlboro journeyed to Chirfa.
  In early winter, Marlboro could not recruit Garrison in Chirfa because 
Uga-Buga Makumb does not own that province, and mercenaries weren't 
available.  So, Marlboro worked hard on his Navigation but was thwarted in 
his efforts.

  Thy humble servant,   Mortimer, Squire to Marlboro


From: Kari
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  In spring, I cast a Plague spell.  Maicuru was hit by a plague.  The 
Plague affected no armies in Maicuru.  Kari's experience raised my prowess 
in Necromancy.
  Your characters of this high level gain the following Advanced Ability: 
  NECROMANCY- "GATE DEMON" SPELL (abbreviated "GD"):  By the dark power of 
this spell, an extra-dimensional gate is opened to the nether worlds, from 
where a demon is summoned to fight in place of the spellcaster.  The caster 
has no control over what type of demon will appear.  If the Demon wins, it 
will return to the Abyss from whence it came.  If it loses, the caster must 
continue the fight at the current combat range.  If another Mirror Image or 
Gate Demon spell is cast against it, both spells will be nullified.  A Demon 
may refuse to fight an opponent of Evil to Undead alignment (50% chance).  
Note: with old Saga programs, order this spell with "GI 28".

  Windy spring was followed by early summer.  I journeyed to Bam Yanga.  
Viewing the southeastern horizon, one can see a Desert province called Abu 
Matariq (#106).  It is said that Bradipo I is the ruler there.  It is known 
to be populated by Humans.  Their Human warriors traditionally array 
themselves as Phalanx and Camel Corps.  To the southwest there lies a Desert 
province known as Apurimac (#1806), a land of Dwarves where Agesilao reigns. 
Their Dwarven warriors prefer to fight in the style of Axemen and 
Camel Corps.  West of here is Ahdogast (#1805), a Jungle area owned by 
no one, where Mermen dwell.  If need be, they can call on a host of Mermen 
to defend their territory.
  With the coming of the late summer season I could find no soldiers in Bam 
Yanga for the requested Trolls troops.  I recruited a rough band of 
mercenary soldiers in Bam Yanga who are known as the 183rd Trolls.

  In Bam Yanga, Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll brought to bay the forces 
of Giovanna.  Kari's forces encountered little resistance in Bam Yanga and I 
there established our rule.  Bam Yanga was discovered to have a tax base of 2
gold.
  The summer mellowed into a colorful fall.  I cast a Skeletal Army spell 
and no skeletons answered the spell's call.
  With the advent of the early winter season, I marched on Ahdogast (#1805) 
with my command.  Southwest of here is the Sahuagin Sea (#1706), a 
prosperous Desert province owned by Agesilao, where Humans dwell.  Their 
Human fighters fight in the style of Camel Corps and Fleet.  To the west 
there is a Sea province known as the Killer Frog Sea (#1705), an area of no 
races where Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango rules.  Viewing the northwest
ern horizon, one can see a Mountain province known as Cascadia (#1704).  It 
is said that Giovanna reigns there.  It is known to be populated by Humans.  
Their Human warriors array themselves in the style of Legion and Fleet.

  Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll's minions initiated a campaign of 
conquest in Ahdogast, a Jungle province owing allegiance to the provincial 
Merman chieftain.  I commanded the invading armies.  The defending forces 
were led by the provincial Merman chieftain.  The armies were drawn up into 
lines of battle as shown here:

  ATTACKING ARMY, Battle of Ahdogast (1805):

 183rd/D  
  Trolls  
    01    
----------
    GC    
 200th/A  
  Mermen  
          
    GC    
  201st   
  Mermen  
          
    GC    
  202nd   
  Mermen  
          
  DEFENDING ARMY

  The defenders had the 203rd Mermen in reserve.  I marched with my loyal 
troops, eyes set in terrible resolution.  No generals were present to lead 
the forces of the provincial Merman chieftain.
  No luck or mischance of great significance seemed to affect the overall 
engagement before it commenced.  In this perilous slugging match, I appeared 
to gain the tactical upper hand.
  The Trolls commanded by me were disgusted with my lack of leadership 
ability.
  Across the entire front, the Depleted 183rd Trolls faced the 200th Mermen. 
The 201st Mermen and the 202nd Mermen outflanked the undermanned enemy and 
attacked with full force.  The 183rd Trolls battled the 200th Mermen and 
were sliced and diced like a knife cutting through lard.
  The forces of the provincial Merman chieftain broke through the lines of 
their opposition and were victorious.  The 200th Mermen annihilated the 
183rd Trolls.
  The attacking Kingdom was defeated and turned back in its attempt to 
conquer Ahdogast.  My forces completely destroyed, I escaped alone to Bam 
Yanga.

  Thy humble servant,   Kari


From: Everard
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  With the advent of the spring season, I prepared to quench my thirst for 
glory.  I rode into Ngara.  I encountered no wandering monsters.
  During early summer, I travelled to Limerick.  In my travels, I saw no 
marauding monster.
  Midsummer's night passed and a pleasant late summer came.  I journeyed to 
the Daedalus Sea.  During my travels, I encountered a Red Dragon.  I spoke 
to the Red Dragon with friendly words, and combat was avoided.

  With the coming of the fall season, I moved into Kilkenny.  I found some 
time to investigate Kilkenny while marching.  100% of it has been explored 
to date.  I also found an Ancient Megaliths (#98) in Kilkenny, inhabited by 
the Giant Scorpion.  What treasure may lie there is unknown.  The Giant 
Scorpion is an oversized scorpion of extreme viciousness which can poison 
its victim with the powerful stinger on its tail.  I encountered no monster.
  The fall cooled into the stillness of early winter.  Everard's 
Resurrection spell backfired and I was left covered with psycho-kinetic goo.

  Thy humble servant,   Everard


From: Gunga Din, Squire to Garin
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  With the advent of the spring season Garin prepared to quench his thirst 
for adventure.  He rode into Ngara.  He encountered no monster.
  During early summer, Garin travelled to Tebessa.  While adventuring, he 
encountered no wandering monsters.
  Midsummer's night came and went and a pleasant late summer came.  Garin 
took a deep, nervous draught from his bottle of old vodka, and entered the 
Sacred Rock.  Garin encountered the Gryphon.  Weaving his artful words of 
magic into a mighty Fireball spell, Garin gestured with his hands and 
damaged the Gryphon, inflicting 10 damage points.
  The Gryphon advanced to bow range.  Weaving his artful words of magic into 
a great Ice Suspension spell, Garin waved his hands, and a shell of ice 
formed around the Gryphon.  The Gryphon crashed, taking 5 damage points.  
Now the effects of the stun wore off and the Gryphon prepared to renew its 
attack.  Casting a Hand Of Death spell, Garin directed scintillating, 
writhing strands of magic and began making squeezing motions with his hands.
  The Gryphon closed to melee range, filled with blood-lust.  Undaunted, 
the Gryphon moved closer and clawed at Garin but Garin evaded the talons.  
The invisible hands of Garin grabbed its lungs, squeezing the breath out of 
the Gryphon and damaged the Gryphon, inflicting 3 damage points.  
The Gryphon assailed Garin and would have hit him if Garin hadn't ducked.  
His unseen fingers pierced the forehead of the Gryphon and clawed at its 
brain and walloped the Gryphon with 3 damage points.  The Gryphon staggered, 
stunned by the force of the deadly blow.  Garin sacked the treasure of 
the Gryphon.  Garin secured the Flaming Scimitar.  He examined the Flaming 
Scimitar and discovered the following properties:
  The Flaming Scimitar has a +20% chance to hit and does +3 damage.  Each 
time it hits an opponent, there is a 5% chance that the tip of the sword 
will release a fireball which implodes in the innards of that opponent, 
resulting in instant death.
  Garin looted 1 gold from the treasure of the Gryphon.
  Garin saw nothing special while scouting out the Sacred Rock.  In his 
travels, he encountered no wandering monster.
  The summer mellowed into a colorful fall.  Garin rode into Limerick.  
While adventuring, he saw no marauding monster.
  With the advent of the early winter season, Garin travelled to Berga.  He 
encountered no monster.

  Thy humble servant,   Gunga Din, Squire to Garin


From: Gladstone
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  In spring, I failed in my attempt to cast a Phantasmal Armies spell.
  The wet spring was followed by a fragrant early summer.  I attempted an 
Illusory Terrain spell, but botched it.
  In late summer, I commanded the 0th Garrison and the 1st Garrison to stay 
behind in Quantara Roo with the provincial garrison commander.
  With the coming of the fall season, I rode into Rejaf.
  The fall darkened into the stillness of early winter.  I cast a Illusory 
Terrain spell and the Plain terrain of Kajaani was magically made to appear 
as Forest.  My experience raised my aptitude in Illusions.

  Thy humble servant,   Gladstone


From: Ningarl
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  With the advent of the spring season, I prepared to quench my thirst for 
glory.  I journeyed to Cretacia.
  During early summer, I levied the 67th Garrison and the 128th Garrison 
from among the people of Cretacia, to serve under me.
  Midsummer's night came and went and late summer came.  I marched my 
command into Silvermist (#502).
  With the coming of the fall season, I cast a Bless spell.  Cretacia was 
magically blessed and prospered.  The skeletal remains of the 48th Chariots, 
the 216th Axemen and the 227th Light Cavalry were Blessed and permanently 
destroyed.
  In early winter, Ningarl's Bless spell fizzled and I wound up covered with 
psycho-kinetic goo.  My efforts improved my skill in White Magic.

  Thy humble servant,   Ningarl


From: Dreux
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  Winter gave way to spring.  I announced a call for volunteers in Birchwood 
and was able to enlist the 343rd Garrison and the 15th Garrison to fight for 
the provincial garrison commander.
  With the coming of the early summer season I explored Birchwood 
thoroughly, leaving no stone unturned, and our exploration level there has 
risen to 61%.
  In late summer, I explored Birchwood well and now 91% of it has been 
explored.  I located a heretofore unknown Temple (#5) in Birchwood, 
inhabited by the Hydra.  Legend says the Antennae of Psychic Blasting is 
hidden here.  The Hydra is a powerful reptilian monster with many 
snake-heads which inhabits swamplands.  I discovered an interesting feature 
in Birchwood: an Altar (#10) inhabited by the Sphinx.  What treasure may lie 
there is unknown.  Legend says that the Sphinx is a powerful winged monster 
with the body of a lion and the head of a man.  The Sphinx is very 
intelligent and loves to riddle.
  The summer surrendered to the fall.  I travelled about Birchwood, 
exploring its features.  After my exploration efforts, 100% of it has been 
explored to date.
  With the advent of the early winter season, I tried to explore Birchwood 
but it seemed that it had already been completely explored.

  Thy humble servant,   Dreux


From: Charious
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  In spring, I travelled to Bir Nzaran.
  Windy spring was followed by a fragrant early summer.  I enlisted enough 
men in Bir Nzaran to form the 129th Garrison and the 178th Garrison for the 
army of the provincial garrison commander.
  With the advent of the late summer season, I rode into Ravenwood.
  During fall, I recruited the 35th Garrison from among the population of 
Ravenwood, to serve under the provincial garrison commander.
  The fall season cooled into early winter.  I levied the 47th Garrison in 
Ravenwood to serve me.

  Thy humble servant,   Charious


