Royal Air Force           124th Dragons    1   122   206th Dragons    3    81
  As the Royal Air Force, the 124th Skeletal Dragons has won recognition as 
the greatest flying unit in the world.  They command great respect from 
other flying units, who are inspired with a great desire to emulate them.  
Consequently, when the 124th Skeletal Dragons trains other flying units, 
their chance to improve in quality is doubled, and the chance for non-flying 
units is increased by half.

Praetorian Guard          240th Elf Bowmen  1   147   108th Elf Bowmen   3   123
  As the Praetorian Guard, the 240th Skeletal Bowmen has won recognition as 
the land unit most qualified to protect the future World Emperor.  Whenever 
they encamp with other armies, they spend their time telling stories of the 
great battles they have fought.  Their gallantry inspires their fellow 
soldiers to train more intensively, so that when the 240th Skeletal Bowmen 
trains other land units, their chance to improve in quality is doubled, and 
the chance for non-land units is increased by half.

Bravest of the Brave      Teleko           1   115   Gladstone        3    84
  The title of "Bravest of the Brave" is granted to the bravest hero in the 
world.
  As the Bravest of the Brave, Teleko has won fame as the Hero who has faced 
the greatest challenges with unyielding courage and self-sacrifice.  Indeed, 
other men draw courage from his example: when he talks to any Hero, that 
Hero's temper will increase to the next higher level.  Reminder: you can 
only list one Talk tactic per encounter.



