GENERAL INTELLIGENCE REPORT

Kingdom of Babba Sissoko (#0):
  From Presto:  In fall, Thorus (#45) marched on the Ark Royal Sea (#1306) 
with his formidable forces.
  In spring, Saladin (#14) explored Mare Tarkium.
  In early summer, Saladin travelled to Falkenheim.
  In early winter, Saladin journeyed to Hollabrand.  Saladin was informed by 
some peasants of a perilous feature in Hollabrand previously unknown to us, 
a Glade inhabited by the Dryad.  During his travels, a Renegade Necromancer 
unexpectedly came at Saladin like a bolt from the blue.  But Saladin hailed 
the Renegade Necromancer with respectful words, and a fight was avoided.
  In early summer, Tlazolteotl (#88) rode her flying armies into Orielle.
  A conquering horde owing their allegiance to 
Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango (#0) invaded the province of Orielle, a 
Plain area ruled by Bradipo I (#2).  Tlazolteotl (#88)'s armies took control 
of Orielle practically uncontested.
  In late summer, Tlazolteotl flew over to Waterford.
  A fleet sent by the empire of Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango (#0) 
invaded Waterford, hoping to subjugate that province ruled by Prometeo (#5) 
and made up of extensive Seas.  Tlazolteotl (#88)'s forces experienced 
little opposition in Waterford and Tlazolteotl there established our reign.
  In fall, Tlazolteotl flew into Bam Yanga.
  In fall, Alain (#33) rode his flying armies into Abu Matariq.
  An army coming from the empire of Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango (#0) 
invaded Abu Matariq, hoping to subjugate that province ruled by Bradipo I 
(#2) and made up of great Deserts.  Alain (#33)'s forces conquered Abu 
Matariq without any major engagements.
  In early winter, Alain flew into Macondo.
  A host of warriors carried the banner of Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango 
(#0) into the Jungle province of Macondo, ruled by Bradipo I (#2).  Macondo 
was overrun by Alain (#33)'s host.

Kingdom of Bradipo I (#2):
  In spring, Orielle was hit by a plague.

  In early summer, a conquering horde owing their allegiance to 
Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango (#0) invaded the province of Orielle, a 
Plain area ruled by Bradipo I (#2).  Tlazolteotl (#88)'s armies took control 
of Orielle practically uncontested.

  In fall, an army coming from the empire of 
Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango (#0) invaded Abu Matariq, hoping to 
subjugate that province ruled by Bradipo I (#2) and made up of great Desert
s.  Alain (#33)'s forces conquered Abu Matariq without any major 
engagements.

  In early winter, a host of warriors carried the banner of 
Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango (#0) into the Jungle province of Macondo, 
ruled by Bradipo I (#2).  Macondo was overrun by Alain (#33)'s host.

Kingdom of Mugai (#3):
  In fall, Mugai (#3) travelled to Tabora.
  In early winter, a diplomatic furor erupted between the Realms of Mugai 
(whose alliances are too incompatible) and Giovanna (#7), degrading their 
diplomatic relations 1 level(s)!
  In early winter, Mugai (#3) treated with his ally Bradipo I (#2).  Mugai 
(#3) treated with his ally Prometeo (#5).  Mugai (#3) treated with his ally 
II Kahn (#6).  Mugai (#3) urged Giovanna (#7) to improve relations with his 
Kingdom, speaking eloquently of the great advantages of such an agreement.  
After some deliberation, the offer was wisely accepted by Giovanna.  Mugai 
(#3) treated with his ally Circe (#8).  Mugai (#3) treated with his ally 
Agesilao (#9).
  In fall, Samantha (#95) marched on Ngara (#604) with her command.


Kingdom of Prometeo (#5):
  In late summer, a fleet sent by the empire of 
Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango (#0) invaded Waterford, hoping to subjugate 
that province ruled by Prometeo (#5) and made up of extensive Seas.  
Tlazolteotl (#88)'s forces experienced little opposition in Waterford and 
Tlazolteotl there established our reign.
  In early summer, Marlon (#68) stood determinedly at the head of his 
thousands.

  Out on the right outside flank, the 326th Dragons were arrayed against the 
Veteran 258th Legion.  The 326th Dragons soared over the 258th Legion and 
attacked them.  The 319th Eagles swooped down on the 258th Legion and 
attacked without mercy.  On this battleground, the clever commander of the 
326th Dragons thought of an idea.  He dragged a few monks out of a nearby 
monastery and lined them up as human shields.  The 326th Dragons fought with 
the 258th Legion and determinedly plowed into their opponents.
  In the interior lines, the Veteran 323rd Trolls were arrayed against the 
232nd Legion.  The 321st Eagles soared over the 232nd Legion and attacked 
without mercy.  The 323rd Trolls battled with the 232nd Legion and viciously 
crushed them.
  Out on the left outside wing, the Crack 320th Eagles were arrayed against 
the Crack 257th Legion.  The 320th Eagles soared over the 257th Legion and 
attacked them.  The 322nd Eagles swooped down on the 257th Legion and 
attacked them.  In this sector, a few soldiers of the 257th Legion panicked; 
however, they were quickly executed by roving security police, and the 
battle proceeded with little disruption.  It seemed that the 320th Eagles 
would break through and win.
  But the battle was not yet done.  The 320th Eagles carelessly blundered 
into a nest of booby traps and lost some of their best front-line troops.  
Even so, the 320th Eagles battled the 257th Legion and was able to make some 
progress.  His forces completely destroyed, Marlon escaped alone to Mare 
Imbrium.
  In spring, Girard (#15) moved into Cantia.  Girard also found a Dungeon in 
Cantia, occupied by the Werewolf.
  In early summer, Girard journeyed to St Helens.
  In late summer, Girard travelled to Amberleaf.

Kingdom of Kahn (#6):
  In early summer, II Kahn (#6) stood ready at the head of his thousands.

  Out on the right outside flank, the Crack 334th Bowmen faced the Veteran 
188th Bowmen.  The 91st Dragons soared over the 188th Bowmen and attacked 
without mercy.  The 91st Dragons were decimated by the bolts loosed by those 
dangerous Bowmen.  On this battleground, the 188th Bowmen expected to have 
the advantage because they had constructed prepared defenses, but were 
chagrined to find out that their enemy had done the same.  The 334th Bowmen 
battled with the 188th Bowmen and managed to make some progress.
  Within the interior lines, the Veteran 198th Trolls faced the Veteran 
220th Light Cavalry.  The 123rd Eagles soared over the 220th Light Cavalry 
and attacked them.  In this area, some soldiers of the 198th Trolls noticed 
the presence of an encampment of trollops behind their opponents, so they 
lustily concentrated their efforts to break through.
  But might defeat now be snatched from the jaws of victory?  The commander 
of the 220th Light Cavalry decided on a charge.  He moved to the front and 
shouted "Smash the cowards!"   and the 220th Light Cavalry charged 
valiantly.  Even with the 220th Light Cavalry's good luck, the 198th Trolls 
battled with the 220th Light Cavalry and gradually shoved them back.
  In the interior front, the Veteran 206th Dragons faced the Veteran 218th 
Legion.  The 206th Dragons swooped down on the 218th Legion and attacked 
without mercy.  The 102nd Eagles soared over the 218th Legion and attacked 
without mercy.  On this field, the soldiers of the 218th Legion were delayed 
by a muddy field.  The 206th Dragons fought with the 218th Legion and moved 
ahead slowly, battled for every foot of their advance.
  Out on the left flank, the Veteran 333rd Bowmen faced the 16th Legion, who 
were blessed by a band of priests sent by the League of Pagan Clerics, which 
aroused them to a fanatical zeal.  The 249th Dragons swooped down on the 
16th Legion and attacked without mercy.  Here, an officer of the 16th Legion 
perceived a gap in the enemy lines which had opened when they moved around a 
wide rock formation.  Charging into the gap, the 16th Legion gained a 
considerable advantage.
  But would victory yet be snatched from the jaws of defeat?  The 333rd 
Bowmen used wide-headed arrows to slash apart the enemy's catapult engines.  
The 333rd Bowmen fought the 16th Legion and plowed into their opponents.
  In fall, Kahn rode into Mare Ionium.
  In early winter, Kahn treated with his ally Bradipo I (#2).  Kahn (#6) 
treated with his ally Cosmic Herderer Mugai (#3).  Kahn (#6) treated with 
his ally Hokuto (#4).  Kahn (#6) treated with his ally Prometeo (#5).  Kahn 
(#6) treated with his ally Giovanna (#7).  Kahn (#6) treated with his ally 
Circe (#8).  Kahn (#6) treated with his ally Agesilao (#9).
  In spring, the waters of the Angel Sea were magically parted.
  In early summer, Sredna (#99) moved into Peachwood.

Kingdom of Giovanna (#7):
  In spring, Maicuru was hit by a plague.  Sageleaf was hit by a plague.  
The Plague affected no armies in Sageleaf.  Tigerhome was hit by a plague.  
The Plague affected no armies in Tigerhome.

  In early summer, Bam Yanga was hit by a plague.  The Plague affected no 
armies in Bam Yanga.

  In late summer, Kajaani was hit by a plague.
  In early winter, the Plain terrain of Kajaani was magically made to appear 
as Forest.  A diplomatic furor erupted between the Realms of Mugai (#3) 
(whose alliances are too incompatible) and Giovanna (#7), degrading their 
diplomatic relations 1 level(s)!
  In early summer, Rolando (#55) marched into Rejaf from Kajaani to defend 
Rejaf against its would-be conquerors.  Rolando marched with his loyal 
troops, eyes set in grim resolution.  Tiffany (#87) stood ready at the head 
of her thousands.

  Out on the right flank, the Elite 240th Skeletal Bowmen faced the 74th 
Camel Corps.  The 124th Skeletal Dragons soared over the 74th Camel Corps 
and attacked without mercy.  The 240th Skeletal Bowmen fought with the 74th 
Camel Corps and cut them down like beanstalks.
  In the interior front, the Crack 110th Bowmen were arrayed against the 
20th Legion.  The 277th Eagles swooped down on the 20th Legion and attacked 
without mercy.  In this sector, the 20th Legion's opponents were lined up in 
an upslope position.  But the 20th Legion charged them, and because there 
was no counter-charge, the 20th Legion shoved them off the crest and gained 
the upper hand.  In spite of the 20th Legion's good luck, the 110th Bowmen 
fought the 20th Legion and managed to make some measure of progress.
  Within the interior front, the Crack 108th Skeletal Bowmen faced the 21st 
Legion.  On this battleground, the 108th Skeletal Bowmen were slightly 
disrupted by a slippery patch of ground and they joined the fight at a tiny 
disadvantage.  Even so, the 108th Skeletal Bowmen battled the 21st Legion 
and gradually shoved them back.
  Within the interior lines, the Green 292nd Skeletal Legion were arrayed 
against the 244th Light Cavalry.  Here, the 292nd Skeletal Legion were 
inspired by the exhortations of an officer who bellowed "Do you want to be 
remembered as Heroes or despised as cowards?  Charge!  !  !"  Even with the 
292nd Skeletal Legion's good luck, the 292nd Skeletal Legion fought the 
244th Light Cavalry and were bent back by their pressure.
  Within the interior front, the Crack 241st Skeletal Bowmen faced the 239th 
Legion.  In this engagement, the contest was a straightforward bashing match 
determined by the courage of the men themselves in melee combat.  The 241st 
Skeletal Bowmen fought with the 239th Legion and the fighting here proved 
inconclusive.
  In the interior lines, the 109th Skeletal Heavy Cavalry were arrayed 
against the 230th Legion.  The Heavy Cavalry troops charged the 230th Legion 
and they wavered under the initial impact.  Here, the 230th Legion had to go 
through a ford.  But their enemy attacked before the crossing operation was 
completed.  The 109th Skeletal Heavy Cavalry battled with the 230th Legion 
and steadily advanced against them.
  Out on the left outside flank, the 209th Skeletal Warg Riders were arrayed 
against the 276th Light Cavalry.  The horses of the 276th Light Cavalry were 
spooked by the terrible Beasts they beheld.  On this field, the 276th 
Light Cavalry were held off by earthen ramparts built up by their opponents. 
But the 276th Light Cavalry had a giant worm on retainer to undermine it, 
and the 276th Light Cavalry broke through quickly, demoralizing them.  The 
209th Skeletal Warg Riders battled with the 276th Light Cavalry and were 
slowly bent back by their attack.  Rolando (#55) retreated to Kajaani.  
Tiffany (#87) made for the safety of Kajaani with her motley army.
  In early summer, Tiffany marched into Rejaf from Kajaani to defend Rejaf 
against its would-be conquerors.
  In late summer, Tigerhome was magically blessed and prospered.  The Bless 
affected no armies in Tigerhome.
  In spring, Drake (#44) marched on Pearlgate (#1703) with his command.
  In early winter, Adhemar (#28) moved into Damnonia.  Adhemar was informed 
by some peasants of a perilous feature in Damnonia, a Tomb inhabited by 
the Ice Devil.  Adhemar located a previously unheard of Cave in Damnonia, 
inhabited by the Black Dragon.

Kingdom of Circe (#8):
  In early winter, Thrym (#59) encountered Jolin (#37).  Thus did Jolin die, 
a brave end by any standard.

Kingdom of Agesilao (#9):
  In late summer, Apurimac was hit by a plague.


